@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Beam groups after late hooks
+
+The bounded `beam_groups::populate_system` boundary implements pinned original `BeamGroupInter.populateSystem/groupBeams` for a fresh system before rhythm processing. It returns identity-based groups, member order, union bounds and pairwise BeamBeamRelation supports; the candidate state remains available for the next stage. Group identities retain creation order, including gaps from removed merged groups. Original group grade is 1; later contextual grades and staff/chord assignment are outside this boundary.
+
+Stable bounds-top ordering precedes the first pass. Rounded scale thresholds are 0.7 interline overlap, 1.2 interline median distance and 0.065 slope difference. The original grown-bounds prefilter and ordinate early exit are retained. Each beam reuses its first ensemble; the second pass merges all ensembles sharing a beam into the first, preserving member insertion order. Member addition creates all pairwise supports, oriented by registration identity and suppressed for existing exclusions. Hooks and small beams participate in normal system grouping. Singletons remain groups. Existing candidate exclusions are preserved.
+
+Independent pinned-JAR controls cover 103 cases, including threshold rounding at three interlines, overlap and slope limits, chained membership, shared-member group merges, tied ordinate order, hooks, small beams, exclusions and empty input. The 13 original image boundaries run creation, uninterrupted extension, late hooks and group formation before rests/epilog. Native comparisons include membership order, group bounds and support order and endpoints.
+
+Input validation precedes processing. Geometry and fourth-power work bounds keep the subset bounded. Existing ensembles, cue-specific aggregate grouping, rhythm regrouping/splitting, rests, epilog, CLI wiring and full OMR are outside this stage. Full debug/release regressions at the current source remain UNVERIFIED and will run separately.
